%N A398613 Decimal expansion of the midradius of a canonical (dual-uniform) 9-gonal trapezohedron with unit short edge length.
%C A398613 The 9-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 9-gonal antiprism.
%H A398613 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398613/b398613.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398613 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Enneagonal_antitegum">Enneagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398613 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398613 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_06">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 6</a>.
%F A398613 Equals csc(Pi/18)*sqrt(1 + 2*cos(Pi/9))/4 = csc(Pi/18)*sqrt(1 + A332437)/4.
%F A398613 Equals the largest real root of 64*x^6 - 384*x^4 + 12*x^2 + 1.
%e A398613 2.442978617801676995464924039232728900742872589900...
%t A398613 First[RealDigits[Csc[Pi/18]*Sqrt[1 + 2*Cos[Pi/9]]/4, 10, 100]]
%t A398613 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398613 First[RealDigits[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 9}, "Midradius"], 10, 100]]
